sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant MG as Mailgun
    participant WC as MailgunWebhookController<br/>POST /webhooks/email/inbound
    participant WS as MailgunWebhookService
    participant TXRepo as TransactionRepository
    participant MsgSvc as TransactionMessagesService
    participant JrnSvc as TransactionJournalsService
    participant DocSvc as TransactionDocumentsService
    participant S3 as S3StorageService<br/>(AWS S3)
    participant ExtSvc as DocumentExtractionService
    participant Claude as Claude API<br/>(claude-haiku-4-5-20251001)
    participant AIS as AiInteractionsService
    participant DB_TX as real_estate_transactions
    participant DB_MSG as transaction_messages
    participant DB_JRN as transaction_journals
    participant DB_DOC as transaction_documents
    participant DB_AI as ai_interactions

    Note over MG,DB_AI: ══ Inbound Email with PDF Attachment ══

    MG->>WC: POST /webhooks/email/inbound<br/>multipart/form-data<br/>{ sender, recipient: txn-{uuid}@txn.mytcapp.net,<br/>  subject, stripped-text, timestamp,<br/>  signature, token,<br/>  attachment-1: file.pdf, … }

    Note right of WC: multer memoryStorage().any()<br/>parses multipart before guards

    WC->>WC: Verify HMAC-SHA256 signature<br/>sign(timestamp + token, MAILGUN_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_KEY)
    alt Signature invalid
        WC-->>MG: 200 OK (always 200 to prevent Mailgun retry)
        Note right of WC: Reject silently — never 4xx<br/>(Mailgun would retry on non-200)
    end

    WC->>WS: processInbound(payload, files[])

    WS->>WS: extractTransactionId(recipient)<br/>parse "txn-{uuid}" from local part
    alt Recipient does not match txn-{uuid}@... pattern
        WS-->>WC: return (no-op)
        WC-->>MG: 200 OK
    end

    WS->>TXRepo: findOne({ where: { id: transactionId } })
    TXRepo->>DB_TX: SELECT * FROM real_estate_transactions<br/>WHERE id = transactionId
    DB_TX-->>TXRepo: TransactionEntity { id, stage }
    alt Transaction not found
        WS-->>WC: return (no-op)
        WC-->>MG: 200 OK
    end

    Note over WS,DB_MSG: ── Step 1: Persist the email message ──

    WS->>MsgSvc: create({ transactionId, channel: EMAIL,<br/>direction: INBOUND, subject,<br/>bodyText: stripped-text,<br/>providerName: mailgun,<br/>providerMessageId: Message-Id,<br/>providerThreadId: In-Reply-To,<br/>threadKey, receivedAt, stage })
    MsgSvc->>DB_MSG: INSERT transaction_messages
    DB_MSG-->>MsgSvc: TransactionMessageEntity { id }
    MsgSvc-->>WS: message

    Note over WS,DB_JRN: ── Step 2: Journal — email received ──

    WS->>JrnSvc: createEntry(transactionId,<br/>EMAIL_RECEIVED, EMAIL,<br/>"Email received from {sender}",<br/>bodyText, related: message.id,<br/>meta: { from, sender, recipient,<br/>messageId, attachmentCount })
    JrnSvc->>DB_JRN: INSERT transaction_journals<br/>(append-only)
    DB_JRN-->>JrnSvc: ok

    alt No file attachments
        WS-->>WC: return
        WC-->>MG: 200 OK
    end

    Note over WS,DB_AI: ── Step 3: For each attachment ──

    loop For each file attachment
        WS->>WS: Check MIME type against allowlist<br/>(pdf, jpeg, png, tiff, doc, docx)
        alt Unsupported MIME type
            WS->>WS: log warn, skip file
        end

        WS->>DocSvc: uploadFile({ transactionId, stage,<br/>file, documentType: stageToDocumentType(stage),<br/>title: file.originalname })
        DocSvc->>S3: upload(transactionId, stage,<br/>filename, buffer, mimetype)
        Note right of S3: Path convention:<br/>transactions/{txnId}/{stage}/{uuid}-{filename}
        S3-->>DocSvc: { storageKey }
        DocSvc->>DB_DOC: INSERT transaction_documents<br/>{ transactionId, documentType, title,<br/>  fileName, mimeType, storageKey,<br/>  status: UPLOADED, workflowStepId: null }
        DB_DOC-->>DocSvc: TransactionDocumentEntity { id }
        DocSvc-->>WS: doc

        alt MIME type is application/pdf
            Note over WS,DB_AI: ── PDF-only: LLM extraction ──

            WS->>ExtSvc: extractFromPdfs([file])
            ExtSvc->>Claude: messages.create()<br/>system: cached extraction prompt + schema<br/>user: PDF as base64 document
            Note right of Claude: cache_control: ephemeral<br/>on system prompt block<br/>(~10% cost on cache hit)
            Claude-->>ExtSvc: ExtractionResult JSON

            ExtSvc->>AIS: create({ feature:'contract_extraction',<br/>responseText: rawJson,<br/>metadataJson: { extraction },<br/>status:'success', tokenCounts })
            AIS->>DB_AI: INSERT ai_interactions
            DB_AI-->>AIS: AiInteractionEntity { id }
            AIS-->>ExtSvc: interaction

            ExtSvc-->>WS: { result: ExtractionResult, interaction }

            WS->>DocSvc: patchMetadataJson(doc.id, {<br/>  extraction,<br/>  extractedAt,<br/>  pdfSource: 'inbound_email',<br/>  confidenceOverall,<br/>  extractionWarnings<br/>})
            DocSvc->>DB_DOC: UPDATE transaction_documents<br/>SET metadata_json = metadata_json || patch<br/>WHERE id = doc.id

            WS->>DocSvc: setAiInteractionId(doc.id, interaction.id)
            DocSvc->>DB_DOC: UPDATE transaction_documents<br/>SET ai_interaction_id = interaction.id<br/>WHERE id = doc.id
        end

        WS->>JrnSvc: createEntry(transactionId,<br/>DOCUMENT_UPLOADED, EMAIL,<br/>"Attachment received via email: {filename}",<br/>related: doc.id,<br/>meta: { sender, fileName, mimeType,<br/>sizeBytes, documentType, stage, messageId })
        JrnSvc->>DB_JRN: INSERT transaction_journals<br/>(append-only)
        DB_JRN-->>JrnSvc: ok
    end

    WS-->>WC: void
    WC-->>MG: 200 OK { received: true }
